>You can get much the same effect by randomising their equipment.

Their equipment is also dictated by their source material.  Yeenoghu has
a flail.  Orcus has a wand of death.

Actually, there's a thought.  Give Orcus something that comes closer
to representing the sheer terror value of the source mythology's Wand
Of Orcus.  As it stands, the only question regarding his wand is whether
you can kill him before either he empties the bloody thing (and starts
casting spells at you instead) or Mjollnir destroys it.

Hell, *removing his wand completely* would make him scarier than he
currently is.

>Give them a random good weapon, either a non-artifact at +5 to +7
>or a artifact at +1 to +3, random good armour and rings, and
>a random useful wand.

The demon lords and princes, apart from Dispater, are Large, and hence
cannot wear body armour, shirts, or cloaks.

>Some times Orcus might get the +1 Vorpal blade,

Whee. Let's add another instadeath crapshoot to the game.

>silver dragon scale mail,

Which will annoy... primary spellcasters and nobody else, because most
people use a big-arse artifact weapon (ideally Grayswandir) to kill
Orcus.

>jumping boots,

No benefit to Orcus except a point of AC.

>and a wand of lightning,

What, so he can blind the telepathic player character and his
non-telepathic self?

>in additional
>to his intrinsic powers. Other times, he might have a cloak of
>magic resistance,

Again, the only people who would care are spellcasters.  See my comment
about SDSM.

>speed boots,

OK, that might actually be actively dangerous.

>a +7 orcish dagger,

*giggle*

>and a wand
>of create monster - posing a slightly different challenge.

He's already a wizardly spellcaster with a bonus to his spell damage.
Just removing his wand of death would make him a challenge.
